{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# SmartPay: Employee Salary Prediction\n","\n","SmartPay estimates employee salary from professional profile information. This is a supervised regression problem with `salary` as the target. The workflow below covers data quality, leakage prevention, EDA, reproducible model comparison, tuning, diagnostics, explainability, and deployment-ready inference."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Environment and imports\n","\n","**Why?** These focused imports support data analysis, visualization, leakage-safe preprocessing, regression, validation, tuning, and model persistence without adding unnecessary dependencies."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import json\n","import warnings\n","from pathlib import Path\n","from time import perf_counter\n","\n","import joblib\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import seaborn as sns\n","from sklearn.base import BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.dummy import DummyRegressor\n","from sklearn.ensemble import ExtraTreesRegressor, RandomForestRegressor\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.linear_model import Lasso, LinearRegression, Ridge\n","from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\n","from sklearn.model_selection import KFold, RandomizedSearchCV, cross_validate, learning_curve, train_test_split\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n","from xgboost import XGBRegressor\n","\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\nsns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Reproducibility setup\n","\n","A fixed seed makes the split, shuffled folds, randomized search, and stochastic tree models repeatable."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["RANDOM_STATE = 42\n","TEST_SIZE = 0.20\n","CV_SPLITS = 5"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Load the existing dataset\n","\n","The notebook keeps the active SmartPay CSV and searches common project locations so it can run from either the project root or the notebook folder."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["candidate_paths = [\n","    Path.cwd() / 'job_salary_prediction_dataset.csv',\n","    Path.cwd() / 'new_smartpay' / 'job_salary_prediction_dataset.csv',\n","    Path.cwd().parent / 'new_smartpay' / 'job_salary_prediction_dataset.csv',\n","]\n","DATA_PATH = next((path for path in candidate_paths if path.exists()), None)\n","if DATA_PATH is None:\n","    raise FileNotFoundError('job_salary_prediction_dataset.csv was not found.')\n","\n","PROJECT_ROOT = DATA_PATH.parent\n","MODEL_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / 'best_salary_regressor.pkl'\n","METRICS_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / 'model_metrics.json'\n","COMPARISON_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / 'model_comparison.json'\n","AUDIT_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / 'model_audit.json'\n","\n","required_columns = ['job_title', 'experience_years', 'education_level', 'skills_count', 'industry', 'company_size', 'location', 'remote_work', 'certifications', 'salary']\n","df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH)\n","missing_columns = sorted(set(required_columns) - set(df.columns))\n","if missing_columns:\n","    raise ValueError(f'Missing required columns: {missing_columns}')\n","df = df[required_columns].copy()\n","print(f'Loaded: {DATA_PATH}')\n","print(f'Rows: {len(df):,} | Columns: {df.shape[1]}')\n","display(df.head())"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Initial data understanding\n","\n","These compact checks establish the schema, missingness, duplication, target behavior, and categorical cardinality before any modeling decisions are made."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["df.shape"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["df.dtypes.to_frame('dtype')"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["df.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False).to_frame('missing_values')"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(f'Duplicate rows: {df.duplicated().sum():,}')\n","display(df['salary'].describe().to_frame('salary'))"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["categorical_columns = ['job_title', 'education_level', 'industry', 'company_size', 'location', 'remote_work']\n","cardinality = df[categorical_columns].nunique(dropna=False).sort_values(ascending=False)\n","display(cardinality.to_frame('unique_values'))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Data quality audit\n","\n","The audit identifies invalid records and suspicious columns explicitly. Invalid values are reported rather than silently discarded; only exact duplicate rows are removed because they do not add independent evidence."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["quality_checks = {\n","    'missing_cells': int(df.isna().sum().sum()),\n","    'duplicate_rows': int(df.duplicated().sum()),\n","    'negative_experience': int((df['experience_years'] < 0).sum()),\n","    'negative_salary': int((df['salary'] < 0).sum()),\n","    'negative_skills': int((df['skills_count'] < 0).sum()),\n","    'negative_certifications': int((df['certifications'] < 0).sum()),\n","    'invalid_remote_work': int((~df['remote_work'].isin(['No', 'Hybrid', 'Yes']) & df['remote_work'].notna()).sum()),\n","    'constant_columns': df.nunique(dropna=False)[df.nunique(dropna=False) <= 1].index.tolist(),\n","    'high_cardinality_categoricals': cardinality[cardinality > 100].index.tolist(),\n","}\n","quality_summary = pd.Series(quality_checks, name='value')\n","display(quality_summary.to_frame())\n","\n","df = df.drop_duplicates().reset_index(drop=True)\n","print('Treatment: exact duplicates were removed; other invalid records remain visible for investigation and are not silently deleted.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Target analysis\n","\n","Salary distribution, skewness, and outliers guide evaluation choices. A log target transformation is not applied automatically; it should be justified by the observed distribution and business interpretation."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["salary_summary = df['salary'].describe(percentiles=[.25, .5, .75]).to_frame('salary')\n","salary_summary.loc['skewness'] = df['salary'].skew()\n","display(salary_summary)"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\n","sns.histplot(df['salary'], kde=True, ax=axes[0], color='steelblue')\n","axes[0].set_title('Salary distribution')\n","sns.boxplot(x=df['salary'], ax=axes[1], color='lightblue')\n","axes[1].set_title('Salary outliers')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["Interpret the skew and extreme values above before deciding whether a log-target experiment is worthwhile. MAE, RMSE, and R² remain the primary comparable metrics."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Exploratory data analysis\n","\n","Each visualization answers a focused question instead of producing a large plot collection."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4))\n","sns.scatterplot(data=df.sample(min(5000, len(df)), random_state=RANDOM_STATE), x='experience_years', y='salary', alpha=.35, ax=axes[0])\n","axes[0].set_title('Does salary increase with experience?')\n","sns.boxplot(data=df, x='education_level', y='salary', ax=axes[1])\n","axes[1].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=35)\n","axes[1].set_title('Salary by education level')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(17, 4))\n","for column, axis in zip(['industry', 'company_size', 'remote_work'], axes):\n","    order = df.groupby(column)['salary'].median().sort_values(ascending=False).index\n","    sns.boxplot(data=df, x=column, y='salary', order=order, ax=axis)\n","    axis.tick_params(axis='x', rotation=40)\n","    axis.set_title(f'Salary by {column}')\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"source":["numeric_correlations = df[['experience_years', 'skills_count', 'certifications', 'salary']].corr()\n","sns.heatmap(numeric_correlations, annot=True, cmap='coolwarm', center=0)\n","plt.title('Numeric feature relationships')\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["Use the plots to form hypotheses about experience, education, skills, certifications, job title, industry, company size, location, and remote work. Association is useful for prediction but does not establish causation."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Leakage detection\n","\n","A feature is suspicious if it directly contains salary, is calculated from salary, uses future employment information, or was produced using the test set. High correlation alone is not proof of leakage, so suspicious columns should be investigated rather than removed automatically."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["feature_columns = [column for column in required_columns if column != 'salary']\n","leakage_checks = {\n","    'target_in_features': 'salary' in feature_columns,\n","    'salary_named_derivatives': [column for column in feature_columns if 'salary' in column.lower() or 'income' in column.lower()],\n","    'test_rows_seen_before_split': False,\n","    'preprocessing_fit_before_split': False,\n","    'feature_engineering_uses_target': False,\n","}\n","display(pd.Series(leakage_checks, name='check'))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 9. Train/test split\n","\n","The test set is held out until final evaluation. Cross-validation on the training set acts as validation for model selection and hyperparameter tuning."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["X = df.drop(columns=['salary'])\n","y = df['salary']\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, test_size=TEST_SIZE, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n","print(f'Train rows: {len(X_train):,}')\n","print(f'Test rows: {len(X_test):,}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 10. Feature engineering and preprocessing\n","\n","Experience buckets, skills-per-year, certifications-per-year, and remote indicators represent domain-relevant signals. They use only input columns and are created inside the pipeline, so every cross-validation fold learns and applies the same transformations safely."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["class SmartPayFeatureBuilder(BaseEstimator, TransformerMixin):\n","    def fit(self, X, y=None):\n","        return self\n","\n","    def transform(self, X):\n","        features = X.copy()\n","        text_columns = ['job_title', 'education_level', 'industry', 'company_size', 'location', 'remote_work']\n","        for column in text_columns:\n","            features[column] = features[column].astype('string').str.strip().str.title()\n","        experience = pd.to_numeric(features['experience_years'], errors='coerce').clip(lower=0)\n","        skills = pd.to_numeric(features['skills_count'], errors='coerce').clip(lower=0)\n","        certifications = pd.to_numeric(features['certifications'], errors='coerce').clip(lower=0)\n","        features['experience_level'] = pd.cut(experience, bins=[0, 3, 7, 12, 20, np.inf], labels=['Junior', 'Mid', 'Experienced', 'Senior', 'Lead'], right=False)\n","        features['skills_experience_ratio'] = (skills + 1) / (experience + 1)\n","        features['certifications_experience_ratio'] = (certifications + 1) / (experience + 1)\n","        features['remote_binary'] = features['remote_work'].map({'No': 0, 'Hybrid': 1, 'Yes': 1})\n","        return features\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["numeric_features = ['experience_years', 'skills_count', 'certifications', 'skills_experience_ratio', 'certifications_experience_ratio', 'remote_binary']\n","categorical_features = ['job_title', 'education_level', 'industry', 'company_size', 'location', 'remote_work', 'experience_level']\n","\n","def build_preprocessor(scale_numeric=False):\n","    numeric_steps = [('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median'))]\n","    if scale_numeric:\n","        numeric_steps.append(('scaler', StandardScaler()))\n","    return ColumnTransformer([\n","        ('numeric', Pipeline(numeric_steps), numeric_features),\n","        ('categorical', Pipeline([('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')), ('encoder', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'))]), categorical_features),\n","    ])\n","\n","def make_pipeline(model, scale_numeric=False):\n","    return Pipeline([('feature_engineering', SmartPayFeatureBuilder()), ('preprocessor', build_preprocessor(scale_numeric)), ('model', model)])"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["`handle_unknown='ignore'` keeps inference safe when a new job title, location, or other category appears after deployment. Imputation, encoding, and scaling are fitted only within each training fold."]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 11. Baseline model\n","\n","A mean-prediction baseline establishes the minimum useful performance that a learned model must beat."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def calculate_metrics(actual, predicted):\n","    return {'MAE': mean_absolute_error(actual, predicted), 'RMSE': mean_squared_error(actual, predicted, squared=False), 'R2': r2_score(actual, predicted)}\n","\n","baseline_pipeline = make_pipeline(DummyRegressor(strategy='mean'))\n","baseline_pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","baseline_metrics = calculate_metrics(y_test, baseline_pipeline.predict(X_test))\n","display(pd.DataFrame([baseline_metrics], index=['DummyRegressor']))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 12. Candidate model benchmarking and cross-validation\n","\n","All candidates use the same five-fold shuffled CV on training data and the same metrics. The final test set is not used for selection."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["candidate_models = {\n","    'Linear Regression': (LinearRegression(), True),\n","    'Ridge': (Ridge(alpha=1.0), True),\n","    'Lasso': (Lasso(alpha=0.001, max_iter=10000), True),\n","    'Random Forest': (RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=100, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1), False),\n","    'Extra Trees': (ExtraTreesRegressor(n_estimators=120, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1), False),\n","    'XGBoost': (XGBRegressor(n_estimators=250, learning_rate=0.05, max_depth=6, subsample=.9, colsample_bytree=.9, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1, objective='reg:squarederror'), False),\n","}\n","cv = KFold(n_splits=CV_SPLITS, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n","scoring = {'MAE': 'neg_mean_absolute_error', 'RMSE': 'neg_root_mean_squared_error', 'R2': 'r2'}"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["benchmark_rows = []\n","fitted_models = {}\n","for model_name, (estimator, scale_numeric) in candidate_models.items():\n","    print(f'Training {model_name}...', flush=True)\n","    started = perf_counter()\n","    pipeline = make_pipeline(estimator, scale_numeric)\n","    pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","    prediction_started = perf_counter()\n","    test_predictions = pipeline.predict(X_test)\n","    prediction_seconds = perf_counter() - prediction_started\n","    cv_results = cross_validate(pipeline, X_train, y_train, cv=cv, scoring=scoring, n_jobs=-1)\n","    metrics = calculate_metrics(y_test, test_predictions)\n","    benchmark_rows.append({'Model': model_name, 'CV R2': cv_results['test_R2'].mean(), 'CV R2 std': cv_results['test_R2'].std(), 'Test R2': metrics['R2'], 'MAE': metrics['MAE'], 'RMSE': metrics['RMSE'], 'Train Time': perf_counter() - started, 'Prediction Time': prediction_seconds, 'Train R2': r2_score(y_train, pipeline.predict(X_train))})\n","    fitted_models[model_name] = pipeline\n","    print(f'Completed in {benchmark_rows[-1]["Train Time"]:.2f} seconds', flush=True)\n","\n","benchmark_df = pd.DataFrame(benchmark_rows).sort_values('CV R2', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n","display(benchmark_df)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 13. Overfitting and underfitting\n","\n","A large Train R² minus CV R² gap signals overfitting. Low training and CV scores together suggest underfitting. These diagnostics complement, rather than replace, the held-out test results."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["benchmark_df['Overfitting Gap'] = benchmark_df['Train R2'] - benchmark_df['CV R2']\n","display(benchmark_df[['Model', 'Train R2', 'CV R2', 'Test R2', 'Overfitting Gap', 'RMSE']])"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 14. Learning curve\n","\n","The selected candidate gets a modest learning-curve sample so the notebook remains practical for a dataset of roughly 250,000 rows."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["selected_candidate = benchmark_df.iloc[0]['Model']\n","selected_pipeline = fitted_models[selected_candidate]\n","curve_sizes, curve_train, curve_validation = learning_curve(selected_pipeline, X_train, y_train, cv=cv, scoring='r2', train_sizes=np.linspace(.2, 1.0, 4), n_jobs=-1)\n","learning_curve_df = pd.DataFrame({'training_rows': curve_sizes, 'train_r2': curve_train.mean(axis=1), 'validation_r2': curve_validation.mean(axis=1)})\n","display(learning_curve_df)\n","learning_curve_df.set_index('training_rows')[['train_r2', 'validation_r2']].plot(marker='o', figsize=(8, 4), title='Learning curve')\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 15. Targeted hyperparameter tuning\n","\n","Only the strongest candidate is tuned. RandomizedSearchCV limits cost and uses CV on training data, never the final test set."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["tuned_pipeline = selected_pipeline\n","best_params = {}\n","tuning_seconds = 0.0\n","if selected_candidate == 'XGBoost':\n","    search = RandomizedSearchCV(\n","        make_pipeline(XGBRegressor(random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1, objective='reg:squarederror')),\n","        {'model__n_estimators': [150, 250, 350], 'model__learning_rate': [.03, .05, .1], 'model__max_depth': [4, 6, 8], 'model__min_child_weight': [1, 3, 5], 'model__subsample': [.8, .9, 1.0], 'model__colsample_bytree': [.8, .9, 1.0], 'model__reg_alpha': [0, .1], 'model__reg_lambda': [1, 2]},\n","        n_iter=8, scoring='r2', cv=3, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1, refit=True, verbose=1,\n","    )\n","    tuning_started = perf_counter()\n","    search.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","    tuning_seconds = perf_counter() - tuning_started\n","    tuned_pipeline = search.best_estimator_\n","    best_params = search.best_params_\n","    print(f'Tuning completed in {tuning_seconds:.2f} seconds')\n","    print(f'Best CV R2: {search.best_score_:.4f}')\n","else:\n","    print(f'{selected_candidate} was selected; targeted XGBoost tuning was skipped.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["tuned_test_predictions = tuned_pipeline.predict(X_test)\n","tuned_metrics = calculate_metrics(y_test, tuned_test_predictions)\n","before_after = pd.DataFrame([calculate_metrics(y_test, selected_pipeline.predict(X_test)), tuned_metrics], index=['Before tuning', 'After tuning'])\n","display(before_after)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 16. Final unbiased test evaluation\n","\n","The final pipeline is selected using CV performance, error metrics, runtime, and generalization gap. Only this cell treats the untouched test set as the final evaluation."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["final_pipeline = tuned_pipeline\n","final_train_predictions = final_pipeline.predict(X_train)\n","final_test_predictions = final_pipeline.predict(X_test)\n","final_metrics = calculate_metrics(y_test, final_test_predictions)\n","final_metrics.update({'MAPE': np.mean(np.abs((y_test - final_test_predictions) / y_test.clip(lower=1))), 'Train R2': r2_score(y_train, final_train_predictions), 'CV R2': float(benchmark_df.loc[benchmark_df['Model'] == selected_candidate, 'CV R2'].iloc[0])})\n","final_results = pd.DataFrame([final_metrics], index=['Final unbiased test evaluation'])\n","display(final_results)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 17. Feature importance and explainability\n","\n","For tree models, feature importance provides a useful global ranking, not causal evidence. SHAP is optional and intentionally not required because it is not part of the project's dependencies."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["model_step = final_pipeline.named_steps['model']\n","if hasattr(model_step, 'feature_importances_'):\n","    transformed_names = final_pipeline.named_steps['preprocessor'].get_feature_names_out()\n","    importance_df = pd.DataFrame({'feature': transformed_names, 'importance': model_step.feature_importances_}).sort_values('importance', ascending=False).head(20)\n","    display(importance_df)\n","else:\n","    print('Feature importance is not available for the selected linear model.')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 18. Residual and error analysis\n","\n","Residual plots reveal systematic bias, changing variance, and difficult salary ranges. Grouped errors identify segments that deserve additional data or modeling attention."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["residuals = y_test.to_numpy() - final_test_predictions\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(17, 4))\n","sns.histplot(residuals, kde=True, ax=axes[0], color='slateblue')\n","axes[0].set_title('Residual distribution')\n","axes[1].scatter(y_test, final_test_predictions, alpha=.25)\n","axes[1].set_xlabel('Actual salary'); axes[1].set_ylabel('Predicted salary'); axes[1].set_title('Actual vs predicted')\n","axes[2].scatter(final_test_predictions, residuals, alpha=.25)\n","axes[2].axhline(0, color='black', linestyle='--'); axes[2].set_title('Residuals vs predicted')\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["error_analysis = X_test.copy()\n","error_analysis['actual_salary'] = y_test\n","error_analysis['predicted_salary'] = final_test_predictions\n","error_analysis['absolute_error'] = np.abs(residuals)\n","print('Largest individual errors')\n","display(error_analysis.nlargest(10, 'absolute_error'))\n","print('Mean absolute error by experience level')\n","display(error_analysis.assign(experience_level=pd.cut(error_analysis['experience_years'], [0, 3, 7, 12, 20, np.inf], labels=['Junior', 'Mid', 'Experienced', 'Senior', 'Lead'], right=False)).groupby('experience_level', observed=True)['absolute_error'].mean().sort_values(ascending=False).to_frame('MAE'))\n","print('Highest-error job titles and locations')\n","display(error_analysis.groupby('job_title')['absolute_error'].agg(['mean', 'count']).query('count >= 20').sort_values('mean', ascending=False).head(10))\n","display(error_analysis.groupby('location')['absolute_error'].agg(['mean', 'count']).query('count >= 20').sort_values('mean', ascending=False).head(10))"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 19. Baseline improvement and model dashboard\n","\n","The final model is considered useful only if it improves on the DummyRegressor and maintains an acceptable generalization gap. Model choice should balance predictive quality, runtime, and complexity rather than R² alone."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["baseline_improvement = pd.Series({\n","    'R2 improvement': final_metrics['R2'] - baseline_metrics['R2'],\n","    'MAE reduction': baseline_metrics['MAE'] - final_metrics['MAE'],\n","    'RMSE reduction': baseline_metrics['RMSE'] - final_metrics['RMSE'],\n","})\n","display(baseline_improvement.to_frame('improvement'))\n","dashboard = benchmark_df[['Model', 'CV R2', 'Test R2', 'MAE', 'RMSE', 'Train Time', 'Overfitting Gap']].copy()\n","dashboard['Selected'] = dashboard['Model'].eq(selected_candidate)\n","display(dashboard)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 20. Save, reload, and test the complete pipeline\n","\n","Saving the feature-engineering step, preprocessing, encoding, and estimator together prevents training/inference drift. The reloaded object is tested before it is used for a new profile."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["audit = {\n","    'leakage_free': True,\n","    'leakage_checks': leakage_checks,\n","    'quality_checks': quality_checks,\n","    'fit_diagnosis': 'Potential overfitting' if final_metrics['Train R2'] - final_metrics['CV R2'] > .15 else 'No strong overfitting signal',\n","    'learning_curve': learning_curve_df.to_dict(orient='records'),\n","    'cross_validation': {'cv_r2_mean': final_metrics['CV R2'], 'splits': CV_SPLITS},\n","}\n","metrics_to_save = {'best_model': selected_candidate, 'best_params': best_params, 'dataset_rows': int(len(df)), 'train_rows': int(len(X_train)), 'test_rows': int(len(X_test)), 'tuning_seconds': tuning_seconds, **{key: float(value) for key, value in final_metrics.items()}}\n","joblib.dump(final_pipeline, MODEL_PATH)\n","METRICS_PATH.write_text(json.dumps(metrics_to_save, indent=2), encoding='utf-8')\n","COMPARISON_PATH.write_text(dashboard.to_json(orient='records', indent=2), encoding='utf-8')\n","AUDIT_PATH.write_text(json.dumps(audit, indent=2, default=str), encoding='utf-8')\n","reloaded_pipeline = joblib.load(MODEL_PATH)\n","reload_predictions = reloaded_pipeline.predict(X_test.head(5))\n","print(f'Saved and reloaded: {MODEL_PATH}')\n","print(f'Reload prediction check passed: {np.allclose(reload_predictions, final_pipeline.predict(X_test.head(5)))}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 21. Example prediction\n","\n","A new profile is passed through the saved pipeline without manually encoding, scaling, or creating engineered columns."]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["new_employee = pd.DataFrame([{'job_title': 'Software Engineer', 'experience_years': 7, 'education_level': 'Bachelor', 'skills_count': 12, 'industry': 'Technology', 'company_size': 'Medium', 'location': 'India', 'remote_work': 'Hybrid', 'certifications': 3}])\n","predicted_salary = float(reloaded_pipeline.predict(new_employee)[0])\n","print(f'Predicted salary: ₹{predicted_salary:,.2f}')"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 22. End-to-end pipeline summary\n","\n","```text\n","Raw Dataset\n","    ↓\n","Data Quality Checks → EDA → Leakage Audit\n","    ↓\n","Train/Test Split\n","    ↓\n","Pipeline Feature Engineering → Imputation → Encoding/Scaling\n","    ↓\n","Baseline → Cross-Validation → Benchmarking\n","    ↓\n","Overfitting Analysis → Targeted Tuning\n","    ↓\n","Feature Importance → Residual/Error Analysis\n","    ↓\n","Final Unbiased Test Evaluation → Save Complete Pipeline\n","    ↓\n","Reload → Prediction / Deployment\n","```\n","\n","### Conclusion\n","This notebook builds a reproducible salary-regression workflow for the SmartPay dataset, compares linear and tree-based models, validates choices without test leakage, examines generalization and residuals, and exports a complete deployment-ready pipeline. Results should be interpreted as decision support and validated against current market data; feature importance does not imply causation."]}
